SPEC = {"beats": [{"key": "all", "vo": "This man just got paid, and in hyperinflation, his wife has to spend it the minute she gets it. It's Germany, nineteen twenty three. Wait until afternoon, and that money buys less. A loaf of bread cost a few hundred marks at the start of the year. By November... about two hundred BILLION. [curious] So what happened? The government owed war reparations it couldn't pay, so it printed more and more money to pay its bills. But the country wasn't making any more bread. More money chasing the same bread means each mark buys less. Free practice for this on levlprep dot com."}]}
